Gaming Together, Wherever You Are!
 GamePoint is one of the world's leading social game developers, based in the Netherlands. We create cross-platform games and have continued to satisfy every type of gamer for over 20 years. We’ve continued success with GamePoint Bingo, Royaldice, Cardparty, and Wordtornado to name a few. We aren’t finished there and continue to develop new games and products for young and old alike. We operate thanks to a diverse international team of game, marketing, and community developers from around the world. We are looking for new team members to help us grow and keep players happy. Come play with us!
 Position Summary - Technical Artist 
 Working closely with the team to understand the artistic direction, gameplay intentions, and technical capabilities.
 Responsibilities:

- Actively problem-solve art ideas and processes to budget and performance;

- Develop and optimize shaders, materials, and lighting to ensure both visual quality and performance;

- Define staging for our Unity Projects;

- Optimize graphics and layouts and create mock-ups for our Unity Programmer;

- Implement an effective, flexible UI for different mobile platforms;

- Create mock-up interfaces for mobile games;

- Update live events using the Addressable system;

- Constant performance and build size optimisation;

- Create documentation and mentor content developers.

 Who you are:

- You have experience with 2D animation and particle systems in Unity and are familiar with animating 2D assets;

- Experience with Unity and C#;

- Knowledge of shader development (HLSL) and the Unity rendering pipelines (URP/HDRP);

- You have knowledge of technical constraints, optimization, and implementation;

- You know how to prototype, test, and implement new features quickly;

- You’re a proactive learner and eager to develop your skills;

- You have excellent teamwork skills;

- You are fluent in English;

- A portfolio demonstrating all aspects of your skill is required.

 Bonus Skills:

- Experience working in an agile project environment;

- Affinity with casual games;

- Knowledge of and interest in usability and freemium best practices;

- Experience in user interface design on multiple platforms.

 Interested?
